----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Third-party material and pinned dependencies (not vendored; see search/README.md "Reproduce")

* exa-labs/benchmarks (the harness, cloned into search/upstream at commit
  0d817af66fb6c47afb7b097b9f4e40a763b6fc3a): MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Exa Labs. Its README notes
  that upstream datasets retain their own terms: BrowseComp is MIT, FRAMES and DeepSearchQA are
  Apache-2.0, WideSearch is CC0-1.0; BrowseComp is decrypted only in memory and must not be republished.
* ArtificialAnalysis/stirrup (the agent loop, cloned into search/aa-stirrup/.stirrup-src at commit
  c092cee80ce09cd1dfb93aef053296a9ecd9dbb6): MIT.
* Datasets read at pinned revisions from the Hugging Face Hub at run time, each under its own license:
  google/frames-benchmark (Apache-2.0), google/simpleqa-verified (MIT), vtllms/sealqa (Apache-2.0),
  ArtificialAnalysis/AA-Omniscience-Public (Apache-2.0; a byte-identical copy is included at
  search/data/AA-Omniscience_dataset_public.csv so the offline tests run without network; its
  license text and NOTICE are in search/data/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt).
* Verbatim grader prompts reproduced in search/METHODOLOGY.md, search/bakeoff/official_prompts.py
  and search/aa-stirrup/aastirrup/grader_prompt.txt are quoted from the benchmark designers' papers and
  notebooks (FRAMES, SimpleQA Verified, SealQA, AA-Omniscience) for the purpose of faithful
  evaluation; copyright remains with their authors. Vendor prices quoted in search/METHODOLOGY.md are
  the vendors' published list prices as read on the stated dates.
* Adapters for Exa, Perplexity, Parallel, Tavily and Brave are upstream's (exa-labs/benchmarks, MIT)
  and are used unmodified from the pinned clone.
* The stored run records (search/runs/, search/aa-stirrup/runs/) contain questions, model
  answers, judge verdicts and reasoning, scores, costs, latencies and per-record citation counts;
  the URLs, titles and text the search providers returned have been removed (search/runs/EXCLUDED.md).
